                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "WXEJz",
                  "fill": "#1F1B16",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "I build thoughtful software at the intersection of backend systems and developer tooling — the kinds of problems that reward patience and a well-labeled button. My days are spent shaping APIs, untangling state, and making the terminal feel a little less hostile. I care about craft over churn, typography over novelty, and leaving the codebase quieter than I found it. When I am not shipping, I am probably reading man pages for fun — which, apparently, explains this website.",
